mode: "100644"
text: "# What to test, the sprint + two worked examples\n\n## Test-priority list (highest leverage first, in your control)\n1. **Hook / first-frame** (short video) — biggest swing on retention/reach.\n2. **Posting time** — easy to test, often high impact.\n3. **Format** — Reels vs carousel vs photo; long vs short.\n4. **Caption / CTA** — length, opening line, the ask.\n5. **Thumbnail / cover + title** (YouTube/Reels) — CTR lever; on YouTube long-form use native **Test &\n   Compare** (up to 3 titles/thumbnails/combos — a true audience split) instead of sequential posts.\n6. **Hashtags / keywords** — branded vs generic, count, placement.\nAlways tie the choice to the **KPI** you're moving.\n\n## Experiment-design template\n```\nHYPOTHESIS: [variable] change will lift [primary metric] for [audience/platform]\nVARIABLE (one): ...                 CONTROL: same platform/format/topic/length/window\nPRIMARY METRIC: ...                 DECISION RULE (pre-set): B wins if ... \nGUARDRAIL: ... must not worsen      DURATION: >=7d (small acct 2-4 wks)   REPS: 3-5 paired\nREADOUT: native analytics           LOG + NEXT: scale / retire / re-test\n```\n\n## The 30-day sprint\n- **Week 1 — Hooks:** 3 paired posts, same topic category + posting windows; vary only the hook.\n- **Week 2 — First-frame / thumbnail:** 3 paired; vary only the opening visual.\n- **Week 3 — Posting time:** same content, two windows, repeated.\n- **Week 4 — Format or CTA:** 3 paired; vary one.\nAlways have **one test running**; log each; promote only patterns seen across **3–5** reps.\n\n## The testing log (keep it)\n| Date | Platform | Variable | A vs B | Primary metric | Result (effect) | Decision | Learning |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\n## Worked example 1 — hook test on Reels (blunt indie-founder voice)\n```\nHYPOTHESIS: a question-hook beats a stat-hook on saves/reach.\nVARIABLE: first 3s only (A: \"Most freelancers overpay tax.\" B: \"Are you overpaying tax?\")\nCONTROL: same Reel body, topic, 9am window, same week. PRIMARY: saves per reach.\nRULE (pre-set): B wins if saves/reach +20% across 3 paired posts. GUARDRAIL: completion not worse.\nREADOUT: IG Insights. RESULT after 3 reps: B +27% saves/reach -> adopt question-hooks; log it.\n```\n\n## Worked example 2 — posting-time test (warm studio voice)\n```\nHYPOTHESIS: an 8am post reaches our audience better than 1pm.\nVARIABLE: posting time only. CONTROL: same carousel template, topic, caption length; repeat 4x.\nPRIMARY: reach. RULE: 8am wins if reach +15% over 4 paired posts. GUARDRAIL: ER not worse.\nREADOUT: native analytics. RESULT: +9% (below threshold) -> a \"tie\": time isn't the lever here; test format next.\n```\n\nBoth: one variable; pre-set rule + guardrail; controlled context; 3–5 reps; read from native analytics;\nlogged; scaled or dropped honestly. Winners feed `content-recycling`/`social-strategy`.\n"
